Title: Mixer: audio path counters and host API error handling
Repository: boxer (https://github.com/alinebee/Boxer.git)
Date: 2026-10-02
Author: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Base-Commit: 0062fc18e154cde6cef3bf3329be4b0658597e31
Preceding-Patches:
  0001-aros-host-sdl-seam.patch
  0002-aros-config.patch
  0003-mount-colon-paths.patch
  0004-host-sdl3-core-audio-timer-on-sdl3-under-boxer-hos.patch
  0005-mixer-channel-lock.patch
Problem: The audio diagnosis could see only device callbacks and underruns. It could not tell whether the core generated too little, whether SDL refused data, or what the device actually opened. Return values of SDL_PutAudioStreamData, SDL_ResumeAudioStreamDevice/SDL_PauseAudioStreamDevice and SDL_GetAudioDeviceFormat were ignored; SDL2's SDL_PauseAudio returns nothing and was never checked.
Solution: MixerHostStats gains frames_mixed (generated by MIXER_Mix, emulated time), frames_delivered (written into device buffers), callback cadence (cb_gap_max_ms), SDL3 put calls/failures/bytes and the largest queued byte count after a put, pause/resume calls and failures, the device format as opened (SDL2 obtained spec, SDL3 SDL_GetAudioDeviceFormat) and the first API error text. Open, format query, pause/resume and put failures are recorded; all but the put (device thread) are also logged with LOG_MSG. A put failure stops that callback's fill. SDL2 pause is verified with SDL_GetAudioStatus. MIXER_SetHostPaused on SDL2 is a no-op after MIXER_Stop or in nosound mode. The device driver, rate, channels, format and buffer are logged at open.
Platform-Scope: All non-Apple builds of the core, both hosts (BOXER_HOST=sdl2 and sdl3), AROS ABIv11 and mainline v1.
Upstream-Status: local-only
Verification: 2026-10-02: build-core/build-ui sdl2 and sdl3 on ABIv11 and mainline v1; the host race harness still clean with this patch. Runtime: ABIv11 only.
Removal-Condition: When the audio path is accepted and the counters are no longer needed, or with the core.

diff --git a/DOSBox/include/mixer.h b/DOSBox/include/mixer.h
index 9fd60089f3f6737c3455fc1724cd61fa12bf5454..8deb34a85103480881d111195053cc864fe3a1ec 100644
--- a/DOSBox/include/mixer.h
+++ b/DOSBox/include/mixer.h
@@ -106,6 +106,18 @@ struct MixerHostStats {
 	Bit32u overflows;                 // too much queued, dropped/compressed
 	Bit32u freq, blocksize;
 	bool nosound;
+	//Audio path stages (2026-10-02): what the core generated, what it
+	//handed to the host API and whether the API accepted it.
+	Bit64u frames_mixed;              // frames generated by MIXER_Mix (emulated time)
+	Bit64u frames_delivered;          // frames written into device buffers (not silent)
+	Bit32u cb_gap_max_ms;             // longest host gap between two callbacks
+	Bit32u cb_last_ms;                // host ms of the last callback
+	Bit32u put_calls, put_failures;   // SDL3 SDL_PutAudioStreamData
+	Bit64u put_bytes;                 // bytes accepted by SDL_PutAudioStreamData
+	Bit32u queued_max;                // SDL3 stream bytes queued after a put (max)
+	Bit32u pause_calls, pause_failures;
+	Bit32s dev_freq, dev_frames, dev_channels, dev_format; // device as opened (SDL2 obtained / SDL3 device format)
+	char error[96];                   // first host API error, empty if none
 };
 void MIXER_SetHostPaused(bool paused);
 void MIXER_GetHostStats(MixerHostStats *out);
diff --git a/DOSBox/src/hardware/mixer.cpp b/DOSBox/src/hardware/mixer.cpp
index 17732bf9ee2ebac5efe2068091863152b96055d3..7289fac1f48c6f1abfb9389fc0b205b07396ae05 100644
